Adapted text
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  Mira (https://github.com/miracodeai/mira)
      Apache License 2.0
      Copyright the Mira contributors
      internal/prompt/templates/deep_mira_general.md and deep_mira_security.md
      are adapted from Mira's review.jinja2 and security_review.jinja2 at commit
      04d3491, and are the default prompts of nitpick deep-review. They are
      prompts sent to a model as written, so they carry no header; the changes
      made are listed here. review.deep.prompts: nitpick selects this tool's own.

      Changes made: the assistant's name, the Mira-only output fields
      (agent_prompt, key_issues, summary), the cache boundary and the context
      sections this tool supplies elsewhere were removed; the severity scale and
      the category guide were mapped to this tool's severity levels and finding
      classes; the tool names were changed to read_file, grep_repo and
      submit_findings; em dashes were replaced. Mira's per-language footgun lists
      were not included.

